{
  "_comment": [
    "The BotPilot wire contract, by example. Every message Studio can send a pilot client, in the exact",
    "shape it goes out on the socket. Two tests read this file and neither one can see the other's repo:",
    "botmaker-studio's TelemetryWireContractTest serializes real events and asserts they equal these, and",
    "botmaker-pilot's wire.test.ts feeds these through the real client and asserts what it decodes.",
    "Both also assert the SHA-256 of this file, so the two copies cannot drift apart silently: change one",
    "and the other side goes red until it is changed too. Keep the copies byte-identical.",
    "'ts' is stamped from the wall clock at send time; 0 here is a sentinel the Studio test substitutes."
  ],
